    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1362" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aesar</span></b> . <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A name of God among the Etruscans</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Aug. 97</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aesar</span></b> ,
			ăris, m., <i>a
				river in Lower Italy</i>, <i>in the neighborhood
				of Crotona</i>, now <i>Esaro</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 15,
				23</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aesărĕus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>pertaining to the
				Æsar</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 15, 54</span></i>.</div>
